Cream puffs with Chantilly cream
6
Small choux buns filled with vanilla Chantilly cream.
---
Choux pastry
semi-skimmed milk|100|ml
water|150|ml
soft butter|100|g
wheat flour|150|g
eggs|4|pcs

Vanilla Chantilly
double cream|150|ml
vanilla pod|1|pcs
powdered sugar|30|g
---
Preheat the oven to 200°C.
Bring the milk, water and butter to the boil in a saucepan.
Off the heat, add the sifted flour all at once and mix vigorously.
Return to medium heat and dry the dough 1 to 2 min stirring until it pulls away from the sides.
Let cool for a few minutes, then add the beaten eggs little by little until you have a smooth, ribbon-stage dough.

Spoon the dough into a piping bag with a plain tip.
Pipe small choux onto a baking-paper-lined tray.
Brush with beaten egg without letting it run onto the tray.
Bake about 20 min at 200°C, until the choux are puffed and dry. Extend slightly if needed.

Make the Chantilly: split the vanilla pod, scrape the seeds and mix into the cream.
Whip the very cold cream to soft peaks.
Add the powdered sugar at the end to stiffen.

To serve, cut the choux in half.
Pipe Chantilly onto the base, then replace the top.
---
Do not open the oven door for the first 10 minutes or the choux may collapse.
Leave the door slightly ajar at the end to dry them well.
Use very cold cream for the Chantilly.
